 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates the model-supplied input against the tool's declared `inputSchema` (JSON Schema, via `ajv`) before calling the executor. Required fields missing or typed incorrectly return a `ToolResponse` describing what failed so the model can retry within the existing tool-round budget — the executor is never invoked for invalid input. Static tool schemas are compiled once at `register` time (a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws at registration, naming the tool); function-valued schemas are validated against the schema returned for the current call. Extra properties pass through to the executor unchanged.
+
+**Migration note:** an executor that used to hand-validate its input now receives only input the schema already accepts. A tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message will no longer see it — the rejection is returned to the model before the executor runs. The version bump is MINOR.
+
